title: configure() guards call log_fatal, which the bundle does not have
updated: 2026-10-25T01:49:23Z
---

Three guards in configure() (lib/Dist/Zilla/PluginBundle/Author/GETTY.pm, lines 1134-1141) call $self->log_fatal:

- weaver_config together with is_task
- author together with no_cpan
- no_install together with no_makemaker

The bundle class has no log_fatal (Dist::Zilla::Role::PluginBundle::Easy does not provide a logger), so each guard dies with "Can't locate object method \"log_fatal\" via package Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::GETTY" instead of its own message. The build still aborts, but the user never sees why.

Reproduce:
  perl -Ilib -MDist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::GETTY -e 'Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::GETTY->new(name=>q{@Author::GETTY},payload=>{no_install=>1,no_makemaker=>1})->configure'

Wanted: each guard aborts with its intended message. The no_license/generate_license guard added in 5fec0ba already uses a plain die with a "[@Author::GETTY]" prefix - bring the three in line with it (or give the bundle one small fatal helper and use it for all four). Add a test per guard that asserts on the message; t/license_file.t has the pattern for the fourth.

